--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Source responsibilities
+
+`cli.mjs` owns the file/terminal boundary: it reads the filename argument, reports
+missing-argument usage, loads newline-delimited JSON while ignoring blank lines,
+and serializes each preview to stdout.
+
+`dispatch.mjs` owns the transformation in `pendingDispatches`: select status
+`ready`, require a nonempty string identifier, then produce `{parcelId, action}`
+records. It performs no file, network or persistence work. Input order is retained.
+
+Data flows from the input file through CLI parsing into the transformation and
+back to stdout. `test/dispatch.test.mjs` exercises the transformation's selection
+and invalid-ID behavior; `test/parcels.ndjson` is the synthetic CLI example.
+Keep I/O in the entry point and selection rules in the transformation. Neither
+module marks parcels dispatched, so rerunning a file repeats its previews.
